# SplashGuard Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root first. It is the single source of truth.

Hard constraints:

- No root, jailbreak, Xposed, or LSPosed. Public Android APIs only.
- No server, account, analytics, crash reporting, or remote config. Only DNS forwarding leaves the device.
- No HTTPS MITM, no URL-path filtering, and never click the ad itself.
- Keep the APK under 8 MB; do not add Room, Retrofit, or other heavy dependencies.
- Every claim needs reproducible evidence. Mark unverified work as "未验证".

Architecture red lines:

- `VpnService` routes DNS targets only. Never turn it into a global VPN or proxy.
- Accessibility is optional and default off. Only small "Skip / Close ad" controls may be clicked;
  both the label node and the final clickable node must pass the size gate.
- Do not listen to `TYPE_WINDOW_CONTENT_CHANGED`.
- iOS ships DNS configuration profiles only. No `NEPacketTunnelProvider` app.
- No database. Storage is assets rules, SharedPreferences, and memory + TSV logs.
- Keep DNS packet, packet building, and rule matching pure Kotlin and JVM-testable.

Before coding: state what you will change, why, and the expected result.
Before finishing: run `./gradlew test`, the 7 accessibility scenarios, and one real cold start
for behavior changes. Never claim "fixed" without verification.

After each major optimization or fix, commit only the related files and run
`git push origin main`. Do not leave large changes only in the local workspace.
